= Price impact =

== Overview ==
'''Price impact''' is the change in quoted or execution prices caused by a trade itself through its consumption of available liquidity or movement of market state.

A larger order generally has greater price impact when available liquidity near the current price is limited. In AMMs, price impact follows from moving reserves along the mechanism's pricing curve.

Price impact should be distinguished from slippage. Slippage compares expected and realized execution and may include external price movement, latency, reordering, or other effects; price impact isolates the trade's own contribution.

Price impact is mechanism- and state-dependent. Two markets with the same displayed price can react very differently to the same order if their depth or liquidity distribution differs.

== Boundaries ==
* price impact ≠ slippage
* price impact ≠ trading fee
* same spot price ≠ same market depth

== Related concepts ==
[[Slippage]], [[Liquidity pool]], [[Automated market maker]], [[Constant-product market maker]], [[Concentrated liquidity]], and [[Liquidity provider]] define the execution context.

